<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chang'an</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chang'an, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian">Xi'an</a>, is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> valley of northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, the capital of several dynasties including the Han and Tang. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> it was one of the largest and most cosmopolitan cities in the world, the eastern terminus of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. It was a focus of diplomacy and conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/changan.jpg" alt="Chang'an" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Tang-era tomb artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prince_Yide%27s_tomb,_towers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
